
# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE ----
# resetMode=loadvm: the 'golden' vmstate lives in disk.qcow2, the station's only
# writable block device (Slackware 3.4 rev-0 ext2 root), so the restore brings back
# BOTH RAM and the filesystem. The GRUB2 boot ISO is attached read-only and is part
# of the device set the vmstate was baked with.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_GOLDEN_STATE_DISK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/slackware/disk.qcow2
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Slackware 3.4 fvwm95 desktop at 1024x768x16: xterm 'darkstar' with a bash# prompt top-left, an 'ICQ - retronet' xterm below it signed in to the museum gateway as UIN 18400 with HiveBot and beos online in the contact list, xclock top-right, FvwmButtons dock bottom-right with a 'web' button that opens Arena on the museum corpus, Start button + taskbar bottom, pointer parked bottom-right. Root logged in (X autostarts from rc.local). Pointer motion absolute through the guest X server (x11warp) over the retronet bridge, buttons + keys over serial mouse / PS/2 keyboard.

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING ----
# XFree86 3.3.1 reads the PS/2 keyboard through the kernel console driver.
# Fleet floor for QEMU keyboard stations (ADD-NEW-OS-PLAYBOOK §0): 40/40.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=40
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=40

# ---- POINTER: ABSOLUTE via x11warp (motion) + Microsoft serial mouse (buttons) ----
# XFree86 3.3.1 offers no absolute device, so the daemon warps the pointer inside the
# guest's own X server. Since the retronet join (2026-09-03) that connection goes
# STRAIGHT OVER THE BRIDGE — 10.99.0.31:6000, the guest's own address on vmbr-rn —
# instead of the slirp hostfwd 127.0.0.1:6084 it used before; there is no slirp on this
# station any more. The guest's session runs `xhost +10.99.0.1` (the bridge address
# labhost sources from); without that ACL every XWarpPointer is silently refused and the
# station falls back to relative motion. Proven 2026-09-03 on the retronet rig with
# scripts/build-guests/tiles/slackware/xwarp.py: warp (100,700) and (900,100) read back
# exact, before AND after `loadvm golden`. The golden was baked with the pointer parked
# at (1020,760) so the ready frame is not confused with a pointer proof.
# TRAP: an X client holding a pointer grab (Arena during its own shutdown) defeats
# XWarpPointer — the warp returns cleanly and the pointer does not move. A one-off
# "MISMATCH" right after closing an app is that, not a broken route; re-run it.
SH_INPUT_BACKEND=x11warp
SH_X11WARP_DISPLAY=10.99.0.31:0
SH_X11WARP_TRACE=off
SH_CURSOR_SCALE=1.0
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60

# ---- BAKE MEASUREMENTS (golden stream, 2026-09-03, slackware-golden branch) ----
# Bake dir /data/vms/sandbox/slackware-golden/bake/, launch.sh = station launcher
# with paths rewritten (same device set: KVM/-cpu host/32MB/pc-i440fx-11.0
# acpi=off/-vga cirrus/sb16/msmouse serial/IDE disk+GRUB2 ISO cdrom).
# Cold boot: fb-wait --settle 10 --timeout 150 -> settled after 31.9s (last
# change at 21.6s); frame /data/vms/sandbox/slackware-golden/bake/fb-cold.png
# matches the reference desktop (xterm 'darkstar' bash# prompt, xclock, dock,
# Start bar) -- same content as /data/vms/sandbox/slackware/smoke/fb10.png.
# savevm golden: VM_SIZE 16.7 MiB, VM_CLOCK 0000:00:42.223.
# Restore proof: relaunch -> loadvm golden -S detected, QMP cont, screendump
# /data/vms/sandbox/slackware-golden/bake/fb-restore1.png = pristine desktop
# (not a cold boot). PASS.
# Keyboard proof: qmp-type 'uname -a\n' into the xterm, screendump
# /data/vms/sandbox/slackware-golden/bake/fb-kbd.png echoes
# "Linux darkstar 2.0.30 #3 Tue Jun 24 03:49:52 CDT 1997 i686 unknown". PASS.
# Pointer proof (golden stream's pixel diff missed it; coordinator re-measured on the
# smoke rig, same device set): the X pointer starts at the screen centre as the 'X'
# root cursor (512,384) and mouse_move carries it 2 px per unit. PASS.
# Reset-is-golden proof: QMP loadvm golden after the keyboard proof ->
# screendump /data/vms/sandbox/slackware-golden/bake/fb-reset.png shows the
# uname output GONE, clock back to bake time -- the restore is the reset.
# PASS.

# ---- RETRONET (phase 3, 2026-09-03, slackware-rn branch) ----
# The station's ONE NIC is a bridge port on vmbr-rn (tap slackwarern0, MAC from
# registry/local.env RN_SLACKWARE_MAC), statically addressed 10.99.0.31/24 with NO
# default route. It carries four things and nothing else:
#   x11warp   labhost -> 10.99.0.31:6000  (the absolute pointer, above)
#   web       guest   -> 10.99.0.2:3128   (Arena; the corpus proxy door, since Arena
#                                          predates the Host: header and cannot use :80)
#   ICQ       guest   -> 10.99.0.2:4000/udp (micq 0.4.3, pre-OSCAR ICQ v5, UIN 18400)
#   exec      labhost -> 10.99.0.31:23    (inetd + in.telnetd behind tcpd; hosts.allow
#                                          lists 10.99.0.1 alone)
# Containment: rn-tapnet.sh installs SLACKWARERN-IN before QEMU starts and the launcher
# runs under `set -e`, so an uncontained guest is not a reachable state.
#
# ---- BAKE MEASUREMENTS (retronet golden, 2026-09-03, slackware-rn branch) ----
# Rig /data/vms/sandbox/slackware-rn/rig/, launch.sh = the station launcher with paths
# rewritten (same device set: KVM/-cpu host/32MB/pc-i440fx-11.0 acpi=off/-vga cirrus/
# sb16/msmouse serial/IDE disk + GRUB2 ISO cdrom/one ne2k_isa on the tap).
# Cold boot: fb-wait --settle 45 --timeout 320 -> settled at 62.0s, last change at
#   16.3s -- the whole desktop, micq signed in and all, is painted 16 s after power-on
#   and then NOTHING on it repaints. Frame rig/fb-cold.png.
# savevm golden: VM_SIZE 17.1 MiB, VM_CLOCK 0000:01:26.825.
# Restore proof: relaunch -> `-loadvm golden -S` detected, QMP cont, screendump
#   rig/fb-restore1.png vs the pre-bake frame rig/fb-prebake.png -> 10 differing pixels
#   out of 786432 (PIL/numpy, full 1024x768x3), all of them one 2x5 block at
#   x=510..511 y=713..717: the dock's xload load-graph bar, which redraws on its own
#   5-second timer. Everything else -- the ICQ window, the terminal, the taskbar, the
#   pointer -- is identical. The only two things on this desktop that ever move by
#   themselves are xload's bar and xclock's minute hand; plan a settle window under
#   60s or expect to catch one of them. PASS.
# Pointer proof after restore: xwarp.py 10.99.0.31:0 100 700 900 100 -> both exact,
#   cursor visible on rig/fb-warp-after-restore.png. PASS.
# ICQ watchdog: `kill` the client in the guest -> icq-session reprints "micq exited;
#   reconnecting in 5s" and micq is signed back in with HiveBot + beos online 6.2s later
#   (rig/fb-icq-reconnect.png). PASS.
# Browser: Arena on http://search.retronet/ (rig/fb-arena.png) and on the corpus site
#   http://home.netscape.com/ with images (rig/fb-arena-corpus.png). PASS.
